    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup features a clear standout in **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who earns an elite 80.98 score. Facing Brandon Pfaadt, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an ideal confluence of variables: a premium #1 spot in the order, a favorable park factor, and\u2014crucially for our SB-weighted strategy\u2014an 86% sprint-efficiency matchup against a pitcher with slow delivery to the plate. Following closely are **Junior Caminero** (74.78) and **Yordan Alvarez** (73.61). **Yordan Alvarez** remains a focal point due to an elite 0.458 xwOBA, while **Junior Caminero** leverages a high-ceiling #3 slot to maximize RBI opportunities against Jobe. These plays provide the stability needed to navigate the challenges posed by tougher arms like George Kirby, who faces **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** today.\n\nStrategic lineup construction required a disciplined approach to the 40-point floor. The most difficult exclusion was **Carson Benge**, whose score of 36.49 fell just short of our threshold. While **Carson Benge** offers upside, his matchup against Harrison (a 3.05 xERA) combined with a detrimental left-on-left platoon disadvantage suppressed his efficiency too far for today\u2019s roster. We are prioritizing players like **Lars Nootbaar** (62.07), who gets a significant boost from a dynamic platoon edge against Clay Holmes. Users should note that our lineup relies on several assumed batting orders; if **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, or **Lars Nootbaar** are shuffled down from their leadoff or #2 spots, their respective scores will contract as the plate appearance projections recalibrate. Monitor the wire for late-breaking news to ensure these key speed-drivers remain in their high-leverage roles.",
